sn42.8:10.1 | S: ‘In many ways the Buddha criticizes and denounces lying, saying: “Stop lying!” | T: the telling of lies, and says, “Abstain from the telling of lies.”
sn42.8:10.2 | S: But I have lied to a certain extent. | T: There are lies that I have told, to a greater or lesser extent.
sn42.8:10.3 | S: That’s not right, it’s not good, and I feel remorseful because of it. But I can’t undo what I have done.’ | T: That was not right. That was not good. But if I become remorseful for that reason, that evil deed of mine will not be undone.’
