## an7.52
an7.52:1.1 | S: At one time the Buddha was staying near Campā on the banks of the Gaggarā Lotus Pond. | T: I have heard that on one occasion the Blessed One was staying near Campā on the shore of Gaggarā Lake.
an7.52:1.2 | S: Then several lay followers of Campā went to Venerable Sāriputta, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him, | T: Then a large number of lay followers from Campā went to Ven. Sāriputta and, on arrival, having bowed down to him, sat to one side. As they were sitting there they said to Ven. Sāriputta:
an7.52:1.3 | S: “Sir, it’s been a long time since we’ve heard a Dhamma talk from the Buddha. | T: “It has been a long time, venerable sir, since we have had a chance to hear a Dhamma talk in the Blessed One’s presence.
an7.52:1.4 | S: It would be good if we got to hear a Dhamma talk from the Buddha.” | T: It would be good if we could get to hear a Dhamma talk in the Blessed One’s presence.”
an7.52:1.5 | S: “Well then, reverends, come on the next sabbath day. | T: “Then in that case, my friends, come again on the next uposatha day,
an7.52:1.6 | S: Hopefully you’ll get to hear a Dhamma talk from the Buddha.” | T: and perhaps you’ll get to hear a Dhamma talk in the Blessed One’s presence.”
an7.52:1.7 | S: “Yes, sir” they replied. Then they rose from their seats, bowed to Sāriputta, and respectfully circled him before leaving. | T: “As you say, venerable sir,” the lay followers from Campā said to Ven. Sāriputta. Rising from their seats, bowing down to him, and then circling him—keeping him on their right—they left.
an7.52:2.1 | S: Then on the next sabbath the lay followers of Campā went to Venerable Sāriputta, bowed, and stood to one side. | T: Then, on the following uposatha day, the lay followers from Campā went to Ven. Sāriputta and, on arrival, having bowed down to him, stood to one side.
an7.52:2.2 | S: Then they went together with Sāriputta to the Buddha, bowed, and sat down to one side. Sāriputta said to the Buddha: | T: Then Ven. Sāriputta, together with the lay followers from Campā, went to the Blessed One and on arrival, having bowed down to him, sat to one side. As he was sitting there, he said to the Blessed One:
an7.52:3.1 | S: “Sir, could it be that someone gives a gift and it is not very fruitful or beneficial, | T: “Might there be the case where a person gives a gift of a certain sort and it does not bear great fruit or great benefit, whereas another person gives a gift of the same sort and it bears great fruit and great benefit?”
an7.52:3.2 | S: while someone else gives exactly the same gift and it is very fruitful and beneficial?” | T: (none)
an7.52:3.3 | S: “Indeed it could, Sāriputta.” | T: “Yes, Sāriputta, there would be the case where a person gives a gift of a certain sort and it does not bear great fruit or great benefit, whereas another person gives a gift of the same sort and it bears great fruit and great benefit.”
